{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>According to all that Elohim commanded him, so he did.</b> Because this parashah begins with the name Elohim, as it is said, ״וַיֹּאמֶר אֱלֹהִים אֶל נֹחַ קֵץ כָּל בָּשָׂר״ — 'And Elohim said to Noah, The end of all flesh' (Genesis 6:13), and it was the attribute of judgment that spoke thus, therefore it concludes with the name Elohim. But the second parashah begins, ״וַיֹּאמֶר ה׳ לְנֹחַ בֹּא אַתָּה״ — 'And YHWH said to Noah, Come you' (Genesis 7:1), and it was the attribute of mercy that spoke thus in saving Noah, therefore it concludes as well with the name of mercy, as it is said, ״וַיַּעַשׂ נֹחַ כְּכֹל אֲשֶׁר צִוָּהוּ ה׳״ — 'And Noah did according to all that YHWH commanded him' (Genesis 7:5). And also what is said in this parashah, ״כִּי לְיָמִים עוֹד שִׁבְעָה אָנֹכִי מַמְטִיר״ — 'For in yet seven days I will cause it to rain' (Genesis 7:4), speaks as well of salvation, to wait for them — perhaps they will return."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:27:30.209250299Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}